From: flip-engineer <will.a.hargis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:29:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/19] Gate only exhausted usage windows and wake
 automatically after the reset (#797, #823)

Exhaustion comes from the latest provider row per window: a limit message or usedFraction >= 1. A partial report with a future reset is open and admitted. The gate evaluates every window, holds on any exhausted future reset, reports elapsed after the reset, and treats a limit message without a reset as unknown without blocking. A held wake schedules one detached single-shot continuation at the earliest reset; it sleeps and re-runs the existing dispatch entry with no new input, the delay is capped at one day, and delivery stays receipt-gated so a handled message gains no second delivery and duplicate continuations leave one delivery and one held report. The query adds the open state. Fixtures cover partial admission, multiwindow hold/elapsed, limit unknown, handled-before-reset, duplicate continuations and the segment cap; each new case fails on c9b65dd58.
